{"id": "3.3-00363", "case_id": "t3.5.s1p.169e2bcb585ba4e7444d.rhs_63f80dd689c76322", "parent_id": "t1.3.s1p.169e2bcb585ba4e7444d", "source": null, "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Round-trip: Stage 1 → generated text → Stage 2</h2><div class=\"stage-grid\"><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 1</div><h3>Write the whole-module specification</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>Clean module RTL: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00363&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>stage1/design.v</a></td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Describe the interface, parameters, and observable behavior of this clean design. Return a self-contained specification, not RTL implementation code. A separate isolated call will receive your specification.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00363&amp;file=stage1%2FTASK.md'>stage1/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Generated whole-module specification (prose).</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage1/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00363&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_04477(DATA0X0,DATA1X0,RESULT0);\ninput DATA0X0; \n input DATA1X0; \n output RESULT0; \n assign RESULT0 = DATA1X0 ^ DATA0X0; \n endmodule</pre></details></div><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 2</div><h3>Repair the module</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>The generated Stage 1 text plus buggy mutant rtl: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00363&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>stage2_template/design.v</a>. Required top module: mg_04477.</td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Repair the functional fault in design.v using the specification and retained RTL context. Return the complete corrected RTL with the same top module. Only the default configuration is scored.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00363&amp;file=stage2_template%2FTASK.md'>stage2_template/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr>